mapping "W6629.1" source="W6629" target="217773000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source W6629 = Swedish-extended ICD-10: SNOMED CT 217773000 The 4th char (2) encodes
        place-of-occurrence (school/institution/public); the 5th char (9) encodes activity
        (unspecified). These 4- and 5-char codes do not exist in international ICD-10 and have no Athena
        crosswalk. Target SNOMED CT 436592 (Accidental drowning or immersion in bathtub, code 217773000) is
        the Athena-mapped standard equivalent of the W66 parent (Athena concept 45756314 436592). The
        target captures the core injury event but does not encode the Swedish place/activity modifiers,
        so the target is broader than the source (target subsumes the injury; source adds place+activity
        detail). Confidence (low): target is plausible and clinically correct for the injury axis, but
        no independent crosswalk exists for these Swedish extensions and the place/activity semantics
        are not represented in SNOMED CT.
        """
}
mapping "W663.1" source="W663" target="217773000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source W663 = Swedish-extended ICD-10: SNOMED CT 217773000 The 4th char (3) encodes place (sports
        facility); no activity char. International ICD-10 W66 has no 4-char subcategory and no Athena
        crosswalk for this code. Target SNOMED CT 436592 (Accidental drowning or immersion in bathtub) is
        the parent W66's standard equivalent. Target captures the injury event; source adds place detail
        the target lacks, so broader. Confidence (low): correct injury target but no independent
        crosswalk for the Swedish extension.
        """
}
